      "extract": "We now summarize the main differences between our scheme and the most recent works on the subject [@ZMHZ10; @HHHLS10]. As noted in [@ZMHZ10; @HHHLS10], the use of Rydberg blocked ensembles allows one to perform entanglement swapping via deterministic manipulations and not through probabilistic photonic detections. The main originality of our proposal is that we also completely got rid of photonic detections during",
